## 2. Standard Per-Application Folder Structure

Every queued target gets an isolated directory `applications/<company-slug>/`:

```text
applications/<company-slug>/
├── resume_tailored.html                       # Role-tailored HTML cloned from plugin resume_template.html
├── <Candidate_Slug>_<Company>_Resume.pdf      # Strict 1-page PDF (zero [TODO: markers)
├── cold_email.md                              # Workflow 3 dossier (only if eligible + verified email)
└── application_state.md                       # Workflow 2/3 state: URL, field map, traps, blockers, status
```

---

## 3. Parallel Worker Scaling Rules (Up to 32 Workers)

1. **1 Worker = 1 Slug:** The coordinator spawns up to 32 concurrent workers, each scoped strictly to one `applications/<company-slug>/` directory.
2. **Read-Only Shared Files:** Workers read `GLOBAL_REFERENCE.md`, `resume/master_profile.md`, and `applications/new_leads.md` **read-only**. Workers never edit `applications/tracker.md` or `GLOBAL_REFERENCE.md` directly.
3. **Blocker Escalation & Single-Writer Merge:** Workers log missing fields, anti-LLM checks, CAPTCHAs, or shady legal clauses in `applications/<company-slug>/application_state.md` and return structured results to the coordinator, which deterministically updates `applications/tracker.md` and Section 4 below.

